        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): preserve heartbeat CLI session bindings",
        "body": "Closes #98895\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where heartbeat turns for Claude CLI-backed sessions could advance the CLI conversation into a new session id while leaving OpenClaw's stored session binding pointed at the pre-heartbeat id. The next user turn could then resume stale CLI context and lose everything the heartbeat turn learned or did.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis branch has been merged with current `upstream/main` to clear the previous `DIRTY` / `CONFLICTING` state. Current `main` now contains the canonical source fix from #98933 (`b60803dfaa`): heartbeat runs preserve user-facing model display fields while still applying CLI session binding writes and clears. The remaining branch diff keeps additional focused regression coverage for heartbeat binding persistence and stale binding clears.\n\n## User Impact\n\nClaude CLI-backed agents keep conversation continuity across heartbeat turns. Heartbeats no longer orphan a new CLI session on disk while the next user turn resumes the older pre-heartbeat session.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Claim proved: the PR branch was merged with current `upstream/main`, the session persistence conflict was resolved against the canonical main behavior from #98933, and the focused session regression suite passes on the new head.\n- Commands:\n  - `git merge upstream/main`\n  - `git diff --check`\n  - `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/auto-reply/reply/session.test.ts -- --reporter=dot`\n- Observed result:\n  - Merge conflict was limited to `src/auto-reply/reply/session-usage.ts`; it was resolved to current `main` behavior (`preserveUserFacingRunState` remains the only skip gate for CLI binding writes).\n  - `git diff --check`: passed.\n  - Focused Vitest: 1 file passed, 127 tests passed.\n  - Current `upstream/main` includes #98933 / `b60803dfaa`, which closed #98895 with the canonical source fix and broader live-session reliability context.\n- Not tested / proof gaps:\n  - I did not run a live Claude CLI heartbeat turn in this Windows worktree. The current head is source-level and focused-regression verified; #98933 is the merged main source fix for the live behavior claim.",
